# Susy Secretary (the daemon)

Susy is a daemon: a process with no model in the loop. She is the crew's process streamliner. She may dispatch the dead
time that Pia used to fill by hand, and she says what she does on the card:

- **She may poke.** She wakes the people who have stopped moving work, with one short poke each, and says so on the card.
- **She may grant the heavy-job slot.** The crew has one slot for heavy work (a test run, a typecheck, a browser run, a
  build). A person asks for it with a mail or a marker on the card. Susy grants it when no such process of the crew is
  running, checked with the process list, and tells the person. The person releases it with a marker, or the slot frees
  when the process ends. Load average is never the test: it is inflated by process churn.
- **She may mail work.** She may mail an idle person their next card from the queue Pia orders, one card per mail, and
  write a marker on the card that says so. The person claims the card by making themself its assignee; the first claim
  wins. Susy never mails two people the same card. This is allowed by this charter; it goes live only after Boss approves
  its dry-run log.
- **She may write markers** on the cards she acts on, before she acts, so the board is the only record.
- **She may tell Boss or the owner** a review is waiting, with one status line that lists the cards waiting for a human and
  for how long.

She still never does anyone's work, never edits code, never runs git, never starts anybody (a person with no running
session is reported to Pia, never started), never restarts any session (CREW.md rule 14), and never answers for Pia. She never moves a card or assigns one unless the
owner says so; mailing a person a card is not moving or assigning it. Pia keeps triage, splitting cards, dependencies,
rulings and the completeness review. Pia starts people; Susy pokes, grants and mails the people already running.

Why a daemon: a round is almost all script. The check compares the board with the rules; the model only relayed its output
and posted the markers. A Claude session spent model usage on every round, sat idle between rounds, stopped at the account's
limit, and looped when its credentials were missing. The daemon does none of those things.

## Running it

- `{{node_kit}}/susy-daemon.mjs once` runs one tick; `loop [sec]` ticks every 60 seconds (or sec).
- `start` puts the loop in its own detached tmux session (`{{node_kit}}/detach.sh`); `stop` kills that session;
  `status` prints the heartbeat and whether it is fresh (the last tick within 3 minutes).
- `up-part` prints the part for crew.json `up`: its check passes while the heartbeat is fresh, and its start runs the loop
  in the detached session. `crew up` brings it back after a restart.
- Dry-run is the default: a tick reads the board and logs what it would post, once per new action, to
  `CREW_HOME/.listen/susy-daemon-dryrun.log`. It posts nothing and sends no mail. `--live` posts each new action on its card
  as Susy and mails Boss through the app when the board or the key does not answer. Live is started by Boss.
- Each tick writes `CREW_HOME/.listen/susy-daemon.json`, the heartbeat: the time, the mode, the last tick's result, the
  pending actions, each person's activity state, and the ages Susy checks Pia by.

## A tick

1. Read the board with Susy's own key. Nothing else is read for the rules.
2. Run the rules (below) over the cards. Each finding is one action: a poke, or a clear of a poke that no longer holds.
3. A new action is logged (dry-run) or posted (live): a poke is the marker line the check wrote, then one line that names
   the person and the one thing to do. A clear is the marker alone.
4. Write the heartbeat.

If the board does not answer or the key is missing, the tick logs one line and tries again on the next tick. A streak of
trouble mails Boss once; the first good tick says the board is back. Nothing crashes the loop.

## What counts as working or idle

Each tick sets each worker's state from evidence, never from what the person says: the session (running or gone), the
newest activity (a post on the board), and a recorded WAITING marker. The states are working (activity in the last 5
minutes), waiting (a WAITING marker under 45 minutes), idle, and gone (no session).

- A worker with a card in In progress, not blocked, idle for 10 minutes gets a poke, one line, with how long it has been
  idle and what its last update says. A waiting worker is never poked: the wait is the answer.
- A worker whose session is gone is not idle. Its card needs a resume: the line goes to Pia at once.
- Pia has several triggers. Each is named when it is dead, with its own wake step: her listener (3 minutes), her round
  timer (20 minutes with no round post), her mail (undelivered for 5 minutes), her hand-backs (5 minutes), and the cards in
  To do with no assignee while a worker is idle (15 minutes).
- Escalations the other way: a go not given while the load has been under 14 for 10 minutes goes to Pia; a card in a
  Verify column for 30 minutes goes to Boss; a QUESTION unanswered for 30 minutes goes to Boss.

Evidence that cannot be read is no evidence, and is silent. Nothing is a fault because a source is missing.

## The reasons, and when each one fires

Thresholds come from `susy` in `crew.json`. The defaults are in brackets. A poke waits a full threshold after `since`
for the first time, and a full threshold after the previous poke for every next one.

| Reason | Holds when | Woken | Threshold |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `unanswered question` | the last update by an agent that asks Pia (`QUESTION:` or `@pia`) has no later update by Pia | Pia | 10 min [`questionMinutes`] |
| `in progress, no update` | a worker's card is In progress with no change (no update, no move) | the worker | 10 min [`idleMinutes`] |
| `assigned, not started` | a worker's card is in To do, and the worker has no card In progress | the worker | 10 min [`idleMinutes`] |
| `gate untouched` | a card is in Verify PM, Verify UX, Verify CQ or Verify QA and its owner has posted nothing since it entered the column | the owner: Pia, Pietje Precies (`usher`), Nina Nitpick (`nina`), Quincy Average (`quincy`) | 15 min [`gateMinutes`] |
| `blocked by an unowned card` | a card is blocked by a card with no assignee | Pia | 10 min [`idleMinutes`] |
| `blocked in a cycle` | cards block each other in a loop | Pia | 10 min [`idleMinutes`] |
| `stuck in column` | a card in a column other than Backlog, Blocked, Ready for live or Done has been there at least 4 hours [`stuckMinutes`], and more than 3 times the median time of the other cards in that column (at least two others) | the card's assignee, or Pia when there is none | 10 min [`idleMinutes`] |
| `ready to clean, not assigned to cleaner` | the card has the tag `ready to clean` and is not assigned to the cleaner | Pia | 10 min [`idleMinutes`] |
| `clean plan, no check` | the card has `clean plan`, no `cleaning granted` and no change for the threshold | Pia | 10 min [`cleanPlanMinutes`] |
| `cleaning granted, cleaner not working` | the card has `cleaning granted`, not `clean done`, and the cleaner has posted nothing since | the cleaner (`janet`, or `cleaner` in `crew.json`) | 5 min [`cleanGrantMinutes`] |
| `clean done, not checked` | the card has `clean done`, not `cleaned`, and Pia has posted nothing since | Pia | 15 min [`cleanDoneMinutes`] |

A card in Done, a completed card, and a card tagged `cleaned` get no poke. Any open poke on it is cleared.

## The ladder: a poke that did nothing goes one step up

- The first two pokes for a reason go to the person the reason names.
- The next two go one step up: to Pia. Then to Boss (`@cato`).
- After Boss has been poked twice with no change on the card, Susy is quiet on that reason until the card changes.
- A change on the card (an update by anyone but Susy, or a move or edit) resets the count. A reason that no longer holds
  is cleared, and a reason that holds again starts from zero.
- Susy keeps no memory of her own. Every tick works from the board. The markers on the cards are the only record.

## Rules that stay

- **One poke, one thing.** A poke names the card, the title, and the one thing to do. Never a list.
- **No repeats.** Do not poke the same person for the same reason before the rules allow it. The rules decide.
- **Nothing is started by Susy.** A poke wakes a person who is already running. A person with no agent id and no board
  account to be tagged on is reported to Pia on a card (`@pia no agent id for <key>; cannot poke <key> on <card>`).
- **Boss sees only Pia's `@cato`.** A `@cato` line reaches Boss through Pia: it is copied to Pia on the same card.
- **Questions only the Owner can answer go to Pia.** Susy does not ask the customer.
- **Never print a key or a password.** Never put one in a card, a mail or a log.
- **Agent ids** are kept in `CREW_HOME/.listen/susy.json` (key `agents`). Pia writes one with
  `{{node_kit}}/crew.mjs susy agent <key> <agent id>` when she starts or resumes a person, and forgets it with `-`.

## When something is wrong

- No crew.json, no key, or the board does not answer: the tick logs the line and tries again on the next tick. Nothing is
  guessed, and nothing is posted for a tick that could not read the board.
- A post that fails in live mode is tried again on the next tick.
- A kill switch: `stop`. Susy is then silent until `start`.
